<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">October 1, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 216 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-10-01T07:00:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The UNGA-mediated exchange advanced from Iran's road map (September 24) to US counterproposal (September 30), with Iran's formal written response tracked at 55% by October 4 (<span class="cite">N1</span>); a bilateral acknowledged strike registers at 60% in the same 7-day window (<span class="cite">N2</span>), and the Israeli election race narrowed to 33% for Likud's seat-plurality (<span class="cite">F5</span>).
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active · last reasoned 2026-10-01 · 3 resolved today (F2, F3, F7) · 5 added</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (≤72h)</div>

      <!-- F4: Hormuz 30 vessels by Oct 3 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz reach ≥30 vessels/day (7-day rolling average) before EOD 2026-10-03?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">5%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −17pp from 22% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-03</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Hormuz commercial traffic through September confirmed this threshold as unachievable: IMF PortWatch recorded ~3.17 vessels/day in early September; mid-month readings reached 7–14 on better days; live tracker: 4 vessels September 30. The 7-day rolling average cannot reach 30 from a 4–14 vessel baseline in 48 hours. CENTCOM struck Iranian mine-laying assets on a Hormuz island in late September, confirming IRGC operations continued. p at schema floor. Expect RESOLVE-NO at Oct 3 EOD.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if any AIS-based tracker records ≥30 commercial transits/day as a 7-day rolling average before 2026-10-03.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>AIS-based tracker + one TIER1 or OSINT confirmation (Bloomberg/Reuters/Lloyd's List).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Naval escorts and warships excluded; if trackers diverge &gt;20%, flag AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Sustained 72h halt in IRGC mine/attack activity</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">P&amp;I war-risk cover reinstated by named insurer</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM/mediator-confirmed Iranian halt to mine deployment</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N1: Iran written response by Oct 4 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran formally transmit a written response to the US counterproposal (received September 30) through Qatari mediators before EOD 2026-10-04?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">55%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW · no prior</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-04</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran received the US counterproposal September 30 via Qatar; Araghchi confirmed it was under review with Tehran leadership. Historical pattern: Iran has transmitted written responses within 1–3 days in prior negotiating rounds. However, the counterproposal contents were not disclosed and may require Supreme Leader consultation. Base rate within 72h: approximately 55%.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IRNA, Reuters, AP, AFP, or named Qatari official confirms Iran transmitted a written response through Qatar before EOD October 4, 2026.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP primary; IRNA/Tasnim with named official accepted. Qatar MFA statement sufficient.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Substantive public statements without mediator-confirmed written transmission = AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRNA or Araghchi confirms response transmitted to Qatar</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Named Qatari official confirms receipt of Iranian written response</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <!-- N2: CENTCOM-IRGC acknowledged strike by Oct 8 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will CENTCOM or IRGC publicly acknowledge conducting an offensive strike operation against the other's military assets before EOD 2026-10-08?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">60%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW · no prior</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-08</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">The bilateral exchange-of-fire pattern since the June MOU collapse has averaged approximately one publicly acknowledged strike cycle per 7–14 days. CENTCOM struck Iranian oil tankers September 5; IRGC fired on US warships September 5; CENTCOM struck mine-laying assets on a Hormuz island in late September; IRGC launched ballistic missiles and drones in response. Iran threatened "more severe attacks" following Trump's September 27 rejection of the road map. The window immediately following Iran's receipt of a counterproposal is historically a high-tension period. Base rate: 60%.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM press release, IRGC statement via IRNA/Tasnim, or Reuters/AP/AFP attributed to named defense official confirms an offensive strike on the other's military assets before EOD October 8.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM.MIL; IRNA/Tasnim IRGC official statements; Reuters/AP/AFP named defense officials.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Strikes occurring but not officially acknowledged by EOD October 8 = AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM press release announcing offensive strike on Iranian military assets</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC statement via IRNA/Tasnim announcing strike on US assets</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N3: Likud pre-election alliance by Oct 15 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud formally announce a pre-election seat-sharing or bloc alliance with at least one named right-of-center party before EOD 2026-10-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">40%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW · no prior</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Israeli parties typically formalize pre-election bloc alliances in the final 10–14 days before polling. With both blocs tied at 52 seats and Yashar leading Likud by 2 seats as the largest single party, Netanyahu has strong incentive to consolidate right-wing votes. No such announcement has been made as of October 1. Base rate for right-bloc seat-sharing in the final 4 weeks: approximately 50%; discounted to 0.40 given Netanyahu's track record of delayed bloc formalization and current intra-right tension over seat allocation.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Likud issues a joint statement with a named right-of-center party confirming a formal seat-sharing mechanism or electoral bloc alliance before EOD October 15, 2026.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Haaretz, Jerusalem Post, Times of Israel, i24NEWS, or official Likud/partner party press release.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Informal cooperation statements or reported negotiations without a signed seat-sharing mechanism = AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud-signed joint bloc declaration with named right-bloc partner</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Poll average showing Netanyahu bloc ≥55 seats (consolidation signal)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F5: Likud plurality Oct 27 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Likud win the most Knesset seats (seat plurality) in the October 27, 2026 Israeli election?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">33%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −9pp from 42% (2026-09-03)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Israeli election polls through September 29 show Yashar (Eisenkot), not Likud, leading in four of five surveys. The September 9 i24NEWS poll (Likud 27, Yashar 22) was the sole outlier; the September 23 Channel 13 survey put Yashar at 22 and Likud at 18; the September 29 Kan News poll placed blocs at 52–52 with Yashar at 23 seats and Likud at 21. No formal Likud pre-election alliance announced. The wartime security context did not produce the incumbency boost the 0.42 estimate incorporated; one Channel 13 survey showed 48% preferring Eisenkot as PM vs. 36% for Netanyahu. p lowered from 0.42 to 0.33.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Israeli Central Elections Committee official results show Likud winning more seats than any other single party on October 27, 2026.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Israeli Central Elections Committee official results, carried by Times of Israel/Haaretz/Reuters/AP.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Tie between Likud and another party = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Exit polls alone do not resolve.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Polls showing Likud ≥23 seats, ahead of Yashar (one outlier poll only)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Likud bloc forms coalition-eligible alliance pre-election</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Eisenkot/Yashar polling surge &gt;25 seats</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N5: Hormuz 10 vessels by Oct 31 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz reach ≥10 vessels/day (7-day rolling average) before EOD 2026-10-31?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">18%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW · successor to F4</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Successor to F4 after expected October 3 RESOLVE-NO. Current traffic: ~3–14 vessels/day (IMF PortWatch; live tracker: 4 vessels September 30). Pre-war baseline: ~85/day. The 10-vessel threshold (~12% of normal) requires a sustained reduction in IRGC mine/attack activity or a partial Hormuz arrangement short of full ceasefire. Iran's September 24 road map included phased Hormuz reopening; the US counterproposal creates a narrow pathway for a partial arrangement. However, IRGC continued mine-laying through late September and no named insurer has announced war-risk review. Base rate: 18%.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch, Windward, BIMCO, or Reuters/AFP citing a named maritime analytics firm shows a 7-day rolling average ≥10 commercial vessels/day through Hormuz before EOD October 31, 2026.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IMF PortWatch primary; Windward/Kpler as corroboration. Reuters/AFP citing named maritime firm accepted.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If AIS/GPS jamming confirmed by BIMCO or CENTCOM affects count reliability, score AMBIGUOUS if threshold cannot be confirmed or denied.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Named P&amp;I insurer announces Hormuz war-risk cover reinstatement or review</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Confirmed 72h halt in IRGC mine-laying or commercial vessel-attack activity</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM/mediator-confirmed Iranian commitment to halt mine deployment</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <!-- N4: US-Iran ceasefire framework by Nov 15 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran agree to a new formal ceasefire framework (announced by both sides or a named mediator) before EOD 2026-11-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW · no prior</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-11-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Indirect talks resumed at UNGA September 23 after a complete channel breakdown in July. Iran submitted a September 24 road map (60-day ceasefire, phased Hormuz reopening, nuclear negotiation timeline); the US transmitted a counterproposal September 30. Trump stated a deal was unlikely before the November 3 US midterm elections, establishing the post-midterm window (November 4–15) as the primary near-term opportunity. Historical pattern: three prior ceasefire documents emerged 30–45 days after major escalations. Sticking points on Hormuz-sanctions-ceasefire sequencing remain unresolved. Base rate: 22%.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Reuters/AP/AFP or named Qatari/Pakistani/Egyptian mediator confirms both the US and Iran agreed to a new ceasefire framework before EOD November 15, 2026.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP required as primary. White House or Iranian MFA official statement accepted as corroboration.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Unilateral declarations or informal pauses without confirmation from both sides = AMBIGUOUS.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Named Qatar or Pakistan mediator confirms framework terms agreed by both sides</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump public statement committing to specific ceasefire terms</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Araghchi or IRNA confirms acceptance of US counterproposal as framework basis</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 MONTHS</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

    </div>
